> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Immaculate Faith. It's going to be a pain in the arse to buy lots of goods from a merchant, nation, farmer if they think you are an ages old abomination out to eat their babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take exception to this statement. Money is money, business is business and as far as the Guild is concerned a Client is a client.<br /> <br /> Nations and Farmers are going to be a bit harder of course, that's why you keep your a lid on your Exalted status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:19:10-07:00","id":288510,"title":"","content":"Another ability of the Lunars that shouldn't be underestimated is their ability to manipulate without revealing themselves. Probably 99.99% of people cannot identify a Lunar that is shapeshifted, and 2E has the following charms: Glance Oration Technique and Falling Leaf Distraction. Those two together allow you to perform Social Attacks without speaking, and making the target think that the idea was their own. As long as you use Essence slowly enough to draw from your personal pool, and not spin up your Anima banner (which would break your shapeshift), you could stroll into a caravan as a cat, and when you walk out the other end, the entire caravan has decided to redirect and head towards your town. Or, heck, you could replace one of their horses, and convince everyone to go where you wanted them to...while still being a horse.<br /> <br /> As for being in The South, and having to deal with no water....well, the Terrestrial Circle Spell 'Water From Stone' solves that problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:25:17-07:00","id":288551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation#post288133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Always on the move. The Sidereals have a Realm wide dragnet, and I'll bet they cast their eyes to the Threshold to ferret out Lunar supply lines and allies. Given time expect Realm/Wyld Hunt/mysterious things taking out your resources. You'd have to constantly keep moving your supply lines around or they WILL be taken out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are overestimating competency and attention here. Sidereals are like a super-understaffed NSA: they may be able to gather a lot of data, but actually analyzing 99.9% of that data is practically impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=288510#post288510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~snip~</div> </div> </div> </div>2e mechanics hiss spit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:38:02-07:00","id":288631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=288551#post288551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are overestimating competency and attention here. Sidereals are like a super-understaffed NSA: they may be able to gather a lot of data, but actually analyzing 99.9% of that data is practically impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that their jurisdiction is <i>all of Creation</i>. Yeah, they're the Chosen of Contrived Coincidence, but with all those billions of square miles of world to cover, much of which is untamed wilderness (and thus solidly the Lunars' home field), it should be pretty easy for a Lunar with any amount of political or financial savvy to set up at least a decent-sized fief before Heaven can take notice, and it should take a fair while for the Bronze Faction to be able to muster any kind of credible response (ie, Terrestrial-lead forces - sending an army abroad is insanely-expensive and time-consuming, although pillaging your target's holdings and living off of the fat of their lands while you besiege them can make it easier). Unless they invoke Sidereal Scry-and-Die Teleporting Deathsquad (with Optional Teleporting Army!) privileges, but bullshit power is bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=288551#post288551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e mechanics hiss spit</div> </div> </div> </div>What about strolling through the caravan as a cat in the dead of night, and breathing portentous nightmares and fever-dreams of obsessive, ruinous glory into the minds of its sleeping masters? Because if there's not some sort of myth-monster that does that, there should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T10:25:02-07:00","id":288668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=288631#post288631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about strolling through the caravan as a cat in the dead of night, and breathing portentous nightmares and fever-dreams of obsessive, ruinous glory into the minds of its sleeping masters? Because if there's not some sort of myth-monster that does that, there should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>YAS ALL THE THISES","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:59:11-07:00","id":289101,"title":"","content":"As an aside, a <a href=\"http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/the-ramree-island-massacre\" target=\"_blank\">historic</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rwblncc3Hgs\" target=\"_blank\">example</a> of nature (or the supernatural) throwing nasty monkeywrenchs in the path of the powers of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:29:44-07:00","id":289124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=289101#post289101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, a <a href=\"http://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/the-ramree-island-massacre\" target=\"_blank\">historic</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rwblncc3Hgs\" target=\"_blank\">example</a> of nature (or the supernatural) throwing nasty monkeywrenchs in the path of the powers of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Welcome to Dzbilchan, motherfuckers.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T01:52:18-07:00","id":289379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation#post288133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> * Lack of easy access to Heaven and it's gods. This hurts more than you think. I'm sure Lunars have friends among the various godly forces but the majority of the big players have to contend with the Sidereal sway in Yu-Shan. This means Lunars are forced to deal with local Elemental Courts, rogue gods, and various &quot;under the table&quot; support they can find.<br /> * The Immaculate Faith. It's going to be a pain in the arse to buy lots of goods from a merchant, nation, farmer if they think you are an ages old abomination out to eat their babies.<br /> * The Threshold may or may not have the resources you need. Being too far in any one direction has it's issues. The extreme west you run into having to deal with ships (His Lunar Excellency must have a &quot;deal&quot; with the Lintha to get ships past the Realm patrols. I swear.) Extreme South is a lack of water, North can kill your followers pretty fast, and the East while friendly in some ways presents poisonous/crazy endless uber trees. You have to pick a middle ground between utility and isolation.<br /> * Always on the move. The Sidereals have a Realm wide dragnet, and I'll bet they cast their eyes to the Threshold to ferret out Lunar supply lines and allies. Given time expect Realm/Wyld Hunt/mysterious things taking out your resources. You'd have to constantly keep moving your supply lines around or they WILL be taken out.<br /> * Charms that may not aid in nation building. Lunars in the 1st Age were build more as combat engines and spies. Unless 2nd Age Lunars are out there developing new charms tied to maintaining and growling civilizations, and I hope they ARE! I'd love to see more Lunar Social charms, then they have issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What is your take on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of these problems aren't too bad actually. You don't have the level of access that Sidereals do to gods, but actually the Silver Pact has had spirit allies for ages, especially in the Bureau of Nature, and in Terrestrial Courts. After all, for like 1500 years any god who didn't like the Bronze Factions' hegemony couldn't turn to the Solars, it was the Lunars who were the enemies of the Bronze Faction. So it's the Lunars who have long-standing alliances. This is probably more with older Lunars than younger ones though.<br /> Secondly, as was said later, it is incredibly easy for a Lunar to not look like a Lunar. Not all, but a lot of Lunars can just look like someone else. So if they are identified by the Wyld Hunt, well, they can just use a new body.<br /> In terms of resources, and being on the move... well, that's the same with Solars. Except Lunars tend to be much more mobile, as most of them can fly. Also, they themselves are quite good at coping with a lack of resources, although that's not something they can really pass on to their human civilisation.<br /> The only big weakness is their charms aren't great for it. But they're not terrible either. The charm for giving people intimacies to their a social group they're exposed to is very useful for making people loyal to the new culture, for example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T20:11:22-07:00","id":290253,"title":"","content":"And having an active support base and training after the Usurpation, unlike the Solars, really helps train new Lunars and Lunar operatives. That might be kinda fun. Playing a Solar who gets trained in Lunar covert tactics. To infiltrate Realm, Guild, and national supply lines to 'acquire' goods, sabotage, and generally be a thorn in the Dragon Bloods side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T20:53:54-07:00","id":290270,"title":"","content":"Would it not be rather difficult for Lunars to train any given Solar in the most elementary tactic they have for covert operations? &quot;Step 1 - hunt your target, kill target, eat target's heart to gain its shape.&quot; Even if Solars can get awesome disguise capabilities in Larceny, learning at the feet of Lunars doesn't exactly help a Solar acquire or reach these methods, since Luna's Beloved just do as they naturally can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T07:12:11-07:00","id":290480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290270#post290270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it not be rather difficult for Lunars to train any given Solar in the most elementary tactic they have for covert operations? &quot;Step 1 - hunt your target, kill target, eat target's heart to gain its shape.&quot; Even if Solars can get awesome disguise capabilities in Larceny, learning at the feet of Lunars doesn't exactly help a Solar acquire or reach these methods, since Luna's Beloved just do as they naturally can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I mean, yeah, obviously being told, &quot;Oh, just turn do what I do,&quot; isn't going to take a Solar very far, but I could see Lunars being very helpful in Solars bettering their skills. Some people learn a lot and learn it quickly from setting themselves up against extreme difficulties in training exercises. If a Solar sets his sights on being able to sneak past someone with the eyes of an eagle or the ears of a fox,* or hear someone as silent as an owl or spot someone as small as a mouse, that will show them a lot of growth in the area. Particularly as the teacher can later give insight into where the screw-ups happened. That Solar is in a much better place to spot or sneak past the Dragonblooded. And that would be if the Lunar stuck only to shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I could also see some Lunars training themselves in the same way. Shapeshifting is always an option and frequently a better one, but staying in human form is sometimes more practical and useful. Their skills in Larceny and Awareness certainly aren't going to make them <i>worse</i> if they apply those as animals, it's just a smaller marginal benefit than Solars would see.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar may or may not handicap himself by excluding &quot;the nose of a wolf&quot; and the like from that list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweaked that first paragraph. 10-23-2014, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T08:57:47-07:00","id":290532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290270#post290270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it not be rather difficult for Lunars to train any given Solar in the most elementary tactic they have for covert operations? &amp;quot;Step 1 - hunt your target, kill target, eat target's heart to gain its shape.&amp;quot; Even if Solars can get awesome disguise capabilities in Larceny, learning at the feet of Lunars doesn't exactly help a Solar acquire or reach these methods, since Luna's Beloved just do as they naturally can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah but Solars have charms that allow them to alter their apperance and take the face of others. Sure they may not have the flexibility of a full blown Lunar face stealer, but if trained by one iy could be the difference between an average Solar spy and a full blown essence Zelig.<br /> <br /> The catch being that the Solar might subvert your networks and contacts after you train him/her to use them. But the force multiplier benefit of such a being as one of your allies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:08:07-07:00","id":290540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290532#post290532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah but Solars have charms that allow them to alter their apperance and take the face of others. Sure they may not have the flexibility of a full blown Lunar face stealer, but if trained by one iy could be the difference between an average Solar spy and a full blown essence Zelig.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. But only if the Solars were good at the necessary skills. Unlike the Lunars, it is not a shared capability and you can't take it for granted that all Solars are awesome at disguises. In fact, most will not be. Ten out of twenty-five is not two out of three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The catch being that the Solar might subvert your networks and contacts after you train him/her to use them. But the force multiplier benefit of such a being as one of your allies... </div> </div> </div>It's no guarantee that a Lunar has Larceny, either. That's part of the problem - they can't teach the Solar a damn thing, because they don't need that thing to operate and don't usually develop it if they don't absolutely need to. And even then, it might not take the Solar nearly as far as they would need to in the realm of non-magical skill in order to develop the magical equivalents. The only Solars that are going to be picking it up quickly without or in spite of your help are going to be the Solars who are already good at it, and they probably have made up their minds about how they're going to use it. This would likely make them hesitant to accept training from someone with a Step 0 that is &quot;be a magical skinchanger.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:07:16-07:00","id":290810,"title":"","content":"Lunars don't have &quot;steal a human's shape&quot; by default either though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:16:54-07:00","id":290813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290810#post290810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars don't have &quot;steal a human's shape&quot; by default either though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:46:39-07:00","id":290824,"title":"","content":"Even assuming they do, which they presently don't, not every Lunar is callous enough to murder a human for their shape either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:54:15-07:00","id":290833,"title":"","content":"I don't think I implied that every Lunar would take advantage of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T18:07:33-07:00","id":290921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290540#post290540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's no guarantee that a Lunar has Larceny, either. That's part of the problem - they can't teach the Solar a damn thing, because they don't need that thing to operate and don't usually develop it if they don't absolutely need to. And even then, it might not take the Solar nearly as far as they would need to in the realm of non-magical skill in order to develop the magical equivalents. The only Solars that are going to be picking it up quickly without or in spite of your help are going to be the Solars who are already good at it, and they probably have made up their minds about how they're going to use it. This would likely make them hesitant to accept training from someone with a Step 0 that is &quot;be a magical skinchanger.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get hung up on the shapeshifting powers. There is no Step 0, it is NOT about what the Solar can't do. It's more about having the right skills at deception, learning about who knows what, and then applying. Remember, the magic may be different but the mission might be the same. And a Solar can be 'good' at something but having a mentor at any skill, developing specialties in quickly switching personalities, and moving through many social circles with ease. That takes skill. And don't forget that a 2 man con tends to work better than one as well.<br /> <br /> Magically, Lunars and Solars are night and day (hehe). But the same skills can overlap. And what Lunar spy is worth his or her salt with out some dots in Larceny? Seriously.<br /> <br /> And no. The Lunar doesn't have to be a face eater. Just really good a blending in and being where they don't belong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T19:05:02-07:00","id":290938,"title":"","content":"I've found that being able to shapechange and infiltrate your way in a small animal is often thwarted by locked doors (I mean, unless you don't mind turning into a hippo and smashing through it, thus alerting everyone around), so being able to turn back into a human and have some Larceny so you can pick the lock is pretty useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290810#post290810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even assuming they do, which they presently don't, not every Lunar is callous enough to murder a human for their shape either.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few ways to get around it, though they're a little awkward. My Lunar's never killed anyone for their forms (it being wrong and all) I paid 4 xp and used the ritual from that knack for hunting other Lunars, to learn 4 human shapes from another Lunar's heart's blood library (but then, that's 4xp down the drain for being moral, and the Lunar I got them from did kill those people), and another human and a raksha commoner's form from sex, with that sex knack. But that itself isn't great (I mean, I could get loads more if I paid prostitutes, but that's kind of immoral) and it's extra xp for all those knacks to be able to do it.<br /> It is possible though.<br /> But it is true, that a lot of Lunars don't have any human forms (in the last game I ran, both Lunars had no human forms beyond their own).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T00:54:35-07:00","id":291852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290270#post290270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it not be rather difficult for Lunars to train any given Solar in the most elementary tactic they have for covert operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally fond of the idea that different people and beings can teach one another, especially Solars, things that aren't directly based on the applicability of their powers, or even entirely in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Just because somebody can't shapeshift doesn't mean that they can't learn something from the tactical doctrine to which the shapeshifting can be applied. It's like how The Art of War is still a useful reference text for strategists, despite how nobody has used chariots in a very long time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T21:34:01-08:00","id":354428,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine Lunars who've been sniffing out organizational vulnerabilities for decades or centuries would be able to pass on a lot of good advice about <b>what</b> exactly the Solars should do to get the effect they want even if the how is significantly different. And their network is likely to have a lot more info about the political state of affairs (albeit from an outsider's perspective) than most other resources starting Solars will be able to get their hands on unless they're being mentored by the Gold Faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T00:35:55-08:00","id":354536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=290270#post290270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it not be rather difficult for Lunars to train any given Solar in the most elementary tactic they have for covert operations? &quot;Step 1 - hunt your target, kill target, eat target's heart to gain its shape.&quot; Even if Solars can get awesome disguise capabilities in Larceny, learning at the feet of Lunars doesn't exactly help a Solar acquire or reach these methods, since Luna's Beloved just do as they naturally can.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars are not mentally-deficient morons. They are more than capable of understanding that others cannot shapeshift and explaining things in ways that do not rely on turning into a shrew. Just because they change into animals does not mean they are retarded canaries. Hell, 80% are specifically predicated on being either smart enough to realize what needs to be taught or sly enough to change tactics when the Solar goes &quot;huh?&quot; - and none of the other 20% have ever been presented as &quot;Hulk smash! Hur-hur-hur!&quot; &quot;Lunar=dumb beast&quot; is on the same level as 1e's &quot;Lunar=Rape Tater&quot;. The Thousand Streams is specifically predicated upon the idea that Lunars are going to be teaching non-Lunars how to live more self-sufficiently over decades, if not centuries. And the TS only works if you assume most Lunars are too dumb to realize how dumb the idea is! So the rather low-IQ option presupposes that a Lunar can quite easily explain how to do things to non-Lunars. Thus any plan even mildly reasonable would, by definition, assume Lunars would be smarter than the TS-yokels, and thus that Lunars are even more capable of interacting with non-Lunars than Tamuz, and Rain Deathflyer, and Silver Python, and Seven Devils Clever, and Strength-of-Many, and .... and every other Lunar, excepting Ten-Stripes (sucked on too many lead-based paint chips as a wee tot) and Leviathan (iPod full of emo-douche crap wedged too tightly in his ears)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:48:27-08:00","id":355034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/288133-thinking-3e-lunar-logistics-and-the-adventures-in-feeding-a-nation?p=354536#post354536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lunars are not mentally-deficient morons. They are more than capable of understanding that others cannot shapeshift and explaining things in ways that do not rely on turning into a shrew. Just because they change into animals does not mean they are retarded canaries. Hell, 80% are specifically predicated on being either smart enough to realize what needs to be taught or sly enough to change tactics when the Solar goes &quot;huh?&quot; - and none of the other 20% have ever been presented as &quot;Hulk smash! Hur-hur-hur!&quot; &quot;Lunar=dumb beast&quot; is on the same level as 1e's &quot;Lunar=Rape Tater&quot;. The Thousand Streams is specifically predicated upon the idea that Lunars are going to be teaching non-Lunars how to live more self-sufficiently over decades, if not centuries. And the TS only works if you assume most Lunars are too dumb to realize how dumb the idea is! So the rather low-IQ option presupposes that a Lunar can quite easily explain how to do things to non-Lunars. Thus any plan even mildly reasonable would, by definition, assume Lunars would be smarter than the TS-yokels, and thus that Lunars are even more capable of interacting with non-Lunars than Tamuz, and Rain Deathflyer, and Silver Python, and Seven Devils Clever, and Strength-of-Many, and .... and every other Lunar, excepting Ten-Stripes (sucked on too many lead-based paint chips as a wee tot) and Leviathan (iPod full of emo-douche crap wedged too tightly in his ears)</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Countermagic. You're a bit late to the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T14:13:03-08:00","id":355107,"title":"","content":"Hmm, given some more detailed statements we've had on what &quot;Solar XP&quot; will entail, I feel even more confident in the idea that a Solar might get something substantial out of learning under a being with different powers. Learning from a shapeshifter might not help with Charms, but imagine the Merits...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}